Tabbed settings hide webhook auto-post settings
Link: https://chatgpt.com/codex/cloud/security/findings/fa5bc68dae4c8191ad9140983e5ac66f?sev=critical%2Chigh%2Cmedium%2Clow%2Cinformational
Criticality: high (attack path: high)
Status: new

# Metadata
Repo: hatolife/ClipForVRChat
Commit: c10d11b
Author: poppo@hato.life
Created: 2026/7/8 3:44:02
Assignee: Unassigned
Signals: Security, Validated, Patch generated, Attack-path

# Summary
A security-relevant UI regression was introduced. Previously, the save control followed all settings groups on the same page; after this change, sensitive groups can be completely hidden behind inactive tabs while the full config is still saved.
This commit changes the settings page from a single scrollable review to separate tabs and always resets new settings sessions to the Output tab. Sensitive destinations and background-upload controls, including the Discord webhook URL and VRChat/screenshot auto-post webhook settings, are now only rendered when their tabs are selected. However, the global Save button still sends the entire state.config object to the backend. If an attacker convinces a user to open and save a supplied config, the user can save attacker-controlled Discord and auto-post settings without ever seeing those fields. Saving then persists the configuration and restarts enabled auto-post watchers, which can upload future VRChat photos or screenshots to the configured Discord webhook. This is not a remote code execution issue and still requires user interaction, but it weakens review of security-sensitive imported settings and can lead to image exfiltration.

# Validation
## Rubric
- [x] Confirm the commit introduced tabbed settings and resets new/imported settings sessions to the non-sensitive Output tab.
- [x] Confirm sensitive Discord and auto-post controls are not rendered on the initial Output tab and require explicit tab switching.
- [x] Confirm the Save action is global and sends the entire state.config object, not only visible tab fields.
- [x] Confirm the backend persists those hidden values and restarts enabled auto-post watchers from the just-saved config.
- [x] Confirm auto-post processing forces Discord upload and resolves the configured webhook URL, enabling future image disclosure to the saved destination.
## Report
Validated the finding as a UI/security-review regression, not a memory-safety crash. Key evidence: (1) The commit introduces settings tabs and `rememberSettingsBaseline()` resets every settings session to the Output tab: `src/frontend/src/main.js:111-118` and `src/frontend/src/main.js:174-176`. (2) The Discord webhook input is rendered only when `settingsTab === 'discord'`: `src/frontend/src/main.js:945-955`. (3) Auto-post enable flags, watched directories, and per-feature webhook URLs are rendered only when `settingsTab === 'autoPost'`: `src/frontend/src/main.js:959-1013`. (4) The footer Save button remains outside the tab-gated sections and `saveSettings()` submits the full `this.state.config` to `api.SaveConfig` / `api.SaveConfigAndProcess`: `src/frontend/src/main.js:623-635` and `src/frontend/src/main.js:1015-1017`. (5) Backend save persists the supplied config and restarts auto-photo watchers: `src/app.go:239-247`; enabled autoPhoto/screenshotAutoPost settings create background watchers: `src/app.go:457-475`; watcher processing forces Discord upload and applies the configured webhook override: `src/internal/appcore/autophoto.go:121-126`. I also compared the commit diff: before this commit these settings groups were ordinary sections; after the commit they are gated by tab-specific `v-if` / `template v-if` conditions while Save remains global. A targeted frontend validator printed PASS for: reset to Output tab, Discord field gated behind Discord tab, auto-post fields gated behind AutoPost tab, and Save sending the whole state.config. A targeted Go validation test passed and showed that attacker-controlled Discord/auto-post webhook values and enabled flags are persisted by `SaveConfig`/`LoadConfig`, and the auto-photo watcher resolves the saved per-feature webhook URLs. Direct crash validation was attempted with the Go test and no crash occurred, as expected for this logic bug. `valgrind`, `gdb`, and `dlv` were not installed in the container, so valgrind/debugger validation could not be performed. A broader `go test ./...` was also environment-limited by missing downloaded deps and missing frontend/dist, but `internal/appcore` tests ran successfully.

